---
const values = [
  {
    title: 'Humanitarian support',
    text: "A portion of this validator's income goes to help people displaced or affected by war, because I've seen what real need looks like.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Transparency',
    text: "I've experienced broken systems. That's why I run this validator openly, responsibly, and without shortcuts.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Community first',
    text: "Being part of Solana means lifting others up. I share what I learn, build what I can, and help where it's needed, especially in Ukraine.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="values">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>What I stand for</h2>
      <p class="lede">These values are not theoretical. I've lived through chaos, through uncertainty, and through war. That's why I care deeply about transparency, people, and building things that matter. This validator is my way of putting that into action, every single day.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="values">
      {values.map((v) => (
        <div class="value">
          <h3>{v.title}</h3>
          <p>{v.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="creed">
      I don't run this validator to maximize my own profits.<br />
      I run it to maximize meaning.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .values {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .value h3 {
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .value p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .creed {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.9rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .values {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
